title: Anni di piombo
subtitle: Italy, 1969–1983
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! if (typeof Q.inflation !== 'number') Q.inflation = 5; if (typeof Q.public_support !== 'number') Q.public_support = 50; if (typeof Q.security !== 'number') Q.security = 50; if (typeof Q.stability !== 'number') Q.stability = 50; if (typeof Q.month !== 'number') Q.month = 12; if (typeof Q.year !== 'number') Q.year = 1969; if (typeof Q.party_name !== 'string') Q.party_name = 'None'; !}

ANNI DI PIOMBO

Italy, December 1969. The post-war political order is under pressure. Strikes and student protests have shaken the country, political extremism is growing, and the bombing in Piazza Fontana has deepened fear and uncertainty.

Lead an Italian political party through the Years of Lead. Your choices will shape public support, economic pressure, public security, and the stability of the Republic.

Choose a party and decide how Italy should face the crisis.

- @party_selection: Begin campaign


@party_selection
title: Choose your party
subtitle: Four political forces, four different paths
new-page: true

Italy stands at a crossroads. Which party will you lead?

- @dc_start: Democrazia Cristiana (DC)
- @pci_start: Partito Comunista Italiano (PCI)
- @psi_start: Partito Socialista Italiano (PSI)
- @msi_start: Movimento Sociale Italiano (MSI)


@dc_start
title: Democrazia Cristiana
on-arrival: {! Q.party_name = 'Democrazia Cristiana (DC)'; Q.public_support = 52; Q.stability = 55; !}

You lead the dominant party of post-war Italian government. Hold together competing factions, maintain coalition support, and respond to demands for reform while defending democratic institutions.

- @monthly_briefing: Enter the political briefing


@pci_start
title: Partito Comunista Italiano
on-arrival: {! Q.party_name = 'Partito Comunista Italiano (PCI)'; Q.public_support = 38; Q.stability = 45; !}

You lead the largest communist party in Western Europe. Build electoral strength, organise workers, negotiate political influence, and decide how to respond to the pressures of the Cold War and domestic unrest.

- @monthly_briefing: Enter the political briefing


@psi_start
title: Partito Socialista Italiano
on-arrival: {! Q.party_name = 'Partito Socialista Italiano (PSI)'; Q.public_support = 24; Q.stability = 48; !}

You lead a socialist party seeking influence between the Christian Democrats and Communists. Coalition bargaining and political reform will define your strategy.

- @monthly_briefing: Enter the political briefing


@msi_start
title: Movimento Sociale Italiano
on-arrival: {! Q.party_name = 'Movimento Sociale Italiano (MSI)'; Q.public_support = 12; Q.stability = 40; !}

You lead a post-fascist party operating on the margins of mainstream coalition politics. Decide how to build support while navigating political isolation and escalating conflict.

- @monthly_briefing: Enter the political briefing


@monthly_briefing
title: Political briefing
subtitle: Italy — month [+ month +], [+ year +]
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! if (typeof Q.month !== 'number') Q.month = 12; if (typeof Q.year !== 'number') Q.year = 1969; !}

THE SITUATION IN ITALY

**Your party:** [+ party_name +]

**Date:** Month [+ month +], [+ year +]

**Public support:** [+ public_support +] / 100

**Economic pressure:** [+ inflation +] / 100

**Public security:** [+ security +] / 100

**Political stability:** [+ stability +] / 100

The Piazza Fontana bombing has intensified public anxiety. The government faces pressure to restore security, address social grievances, and preserve democratic institutions. You have one major political action this month.

Choose your priority. Each decision changes the political situation and advances the calendar by one month.

- @economic_policy: Economic relief and labour negotiations
- @security_policy: Strengthen public security
- @reform_policy: Pursue political and institutional reform
- @wait_policy: Maintain the current course


@economic_policy
title: Economic relief and labour negotiations
on-arrival: {! Q.inflation = Math.max(0, Q.inflation - 5); Q.public_support = Math.min(100, Q.public_support + 3); Q.stability = Math.max(0, Q.stability - 1); Q.month = Q.month + 1; if (Q.month > 12) { Q.month = 1; Q.year = Q.year + 1; } !}

You announce an economic relief programme and open negotiations with labour representatives. The measure offers immediate political benefits, but business groups warn that continued intervention could deepen economic uncertainty.

- @monthly_briefing: Continue to next month


@security_policy
title: Strengthen public security
on-arrival: {! Q.security = Math.min(100, Q.security + 6); Q.public_support = Math.max(0, Q.public_support - 2); Q.stability = Math.min(100, Q.stability + 2); Q.month = Q.month + 1; if (Q.month > 12) { Q.month = 1; Q.year = Q.year + 1; } !}

You prioritise public security and the protection of democratic institutions. Some citizens welcome decisive action, while others warn that emergency measures must not undermine civil liberties.

- @monthly_briefing: Continue to next month


@reform_policy
title: Political and institutional reform
on-arrival: {! Q.public_support = Math.min(100, Q.public_support + 4); Q.stability = Math.min(100, Q.stability + 3); Q.month = Q.month + 1; if (Q.month > 12) { Q.month = 1; Q.year = Q.year + 1; } !}

You pursue political reform, parliamentary dialogue, and a negotiated response to social unrest. Your approach may strengthen trust, although entrenched interests could resist changes to the existing balance of power.

- @monthly_briefing: Continue to next month


@wait_policy
title: Maintain the current course
on-arrival: {! Q.stability = Math.max(0, Q.stability - 3); Q.security = Math.max(0, Q.security - 1); Q.month = Q.month + 1; if (Q.month > 12) { Q.month = 1; Q.year = Q.year + 1; } !}

You postpone major changes and preserve the current political course. This avoids an immediate confrontation, but unresolved pressures continue to build.

- @monthly_briefing: Continue to next month
